From 071eb1aa34902e7b951f17ad64fe49f1ac4ad11a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 05:55:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Solvers of Trilinos: second review

- Ifpack2: the parameters are given to a preconditioner of the chosen type
  built without matrix (the relaxations refuse a misspelt name), instead of
  being checked against Ifpack2::getValidParameters, which does not list
  all the parameters and refused valid ones. The supported types are
  quoted in the error message (some names contain spaces).
- Belos: the parameters, and those of the outer solver of the hybrid
  GMRES, are checked at the creation (Belos only checks them from the
  second call to setParameters, which made the change of the tolerance
  fail).
- Hybrid GMRES: the tolerance, the maximum number of iterations, the
  verbosity and the restart parameters go to its outer solver (Block GMRES
  by default); the relative tolerance is read and changed there; the
  polynomial is built again when the matrix changes.
- MueLu: the names are only checked in the simplified syntax (not with a
  sublist Hierarchy, the facade or the parameters of ML); SPGEMM_KK is
  only set on CUDA.
- CMake: the Kokkos built with Trilinos is also checked, and a warning is
  printed when the Kokkos of Trilinos is not found.
- FROSch: documented as less verbose, not silent.
- Tests: valid parameters of Ifpack2 accepted, all the types of Ifpack2
  created, Schwarz with RILUK, hybrid GMRES, parameters of ML accepted,
  misspelt parameters of Belos refused, FROSch compared to the Jacobi
  relaxation on the elasticity and exact with one process.
---
